From ee49effb097770ac424d49aed1d10591ec50bfa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas Le Bayon <nicolas.le.bayon@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 11:19:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 560/572] plat(stm32mp2): preserve RETRAMCR bits when disabling
 RETRAM erase

Use mmio_setbits_32() instead of mmio_write_32() when setting
SRAMHWERDIS in RAMCFG_RETRAMCR during power management TDCID
initialization.
This avoids overwriting other RETRAMCR bits and only updates
the hardware erase disable bit as intended.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git c34f347d8ccb42bf299b199a5b5f11db6b1c7631 plat(stm32mp2): preserve RETRAMCR bits when disabling RETRAM erase]
Change-Id: I43e4460883d75799ff2eb191ec31324b62e4862d
Signed-off-by: Nicolas Le Bayon <nicolas.le.bayon@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/601734
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Lionel DEBIEVE <lionel.debieve@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Nicolas LE BAYON <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Nicolas LE BAYON <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
---
 plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c b/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c
index ab4fcfcd23..e8aa4440a9 100644
--- a/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c
+++ b/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c
@@ -1628,7 +1628,7 @@ static void stm32_pm_tdcid_init(void *fdt)
 	mmio_write_32(pwr_base + PWR_CR10, PWR_CR10_RETRBSEN_STANDBY);
 
 	/* Prevent RETRAM erase */
-	mmio_write_32(RAMCFG_BASE + RAMCFG_RETRAMCR, SRAMHWERDIS);
+	mmio_setbits_32(RAMCFG_BASE + RAMCFG_RETRAMCR, SRAMHWERDIS);
 
 #if !STM32MP21
 	/* System standby not set (D3) */
-- 
